# Nivo78 Rule Projection — 10-security

**Binding status:** This file is a maintained enforcement projection of the canonical Nivo78 Product Standard.
**Source:** `reference/NIVO78_APP_STANDARD.txt`
**Authority:** The canonical standard and rule-ID catalog control if this projection and the source ever differ.

## Agent instructions
- Apply this rule whenever the work described by the rule is relevant.
- Treat every requirement below as binding unless the canonical standard marks it as `[QA]`/conditional or an approved override applies.
- Preserve and mention canonical `APP-*`, `WEB-*`, `MARKETING-*`, and other rule IDs when reporting compliance or exceptions.
- Do not weaken a requirement merely because it is inconvenient to implement.
- If a requirement cannot be met, stop before shipping and use the standard override process.

---

APPLICATION SECURITY (APP-SEC-\*) — EVERY APP

\================================================================================



APP-SEC-THREAT-MODEL [QA]

\- Each product must maintain a concise threat model
identifying protected assets, relevant threats,

  trust
boundaries, and the controls used to reduce material risks.

\- Review before first release and when material
architecture or data-handling changes occur.



APP-SEC-CRYPTOGRAPHY [GATE]

\- Use established, currently supported cryptographic
algorithms and platform-approved cryptographic

 
implementations. Do not implement proprietary encryption algorithms or
custom cryptographic primitives.



APP-SEC-KEY-DERIVATION [GATE]

\- Passwords used to protect application secrets must
be processed with a modern password-based

  key-derivation
function using a unique salt and parameters appropriate to current security
guidance.

\- Never use a raw password or simple hash as an
encryption key.



APP-SEC-RANDOMNESS [GATE]

\- Security-sensitive tokens, salts, nonces, recovery
material, and identifiers requiring unpredictability

  must use a
cryptographically secure random source.



APP-SEC-SECRET-LIFETIME [QA]

\- Minimize the lifetime of secrets in memory, logs,
temporary files, clipboard contents, crash artifacts,

  and exported
diagnostics. Do not intentionally retain secrets longer than required for the
operation.



APP-SEC-IMPORT-VALIDATION [GATE]

\- Treat imported files, pasted structured data, deep
links, external content, and user-supplied paths

  as untrusted
input. Validate size, structure, encoding, type, ranges, and expected schema
before processing.



APP-SEC-PATH-SAFETY [GATE]

\- File operations must prevent path traversal and
unintended access outside the application's permitted

  data
locations. Never construct security-sensitive paths directly from unvalidated
user input.



APP-SEC-EXTERNAL-CONTENT [GATE]

\- External URLs, files, intents, browser handoffs, and
other external content must be validated and

  handled
explicitly. Do not execute or interpret external content merely because it was
supplied by

  a user or
imported file.



APP-SEC-FAIL-CLOSED [GATE]

\- Security-sensitive failures must fail closed. Do not
silently continue using invalid credentials,

  corrupted
security metadata, unsupported encryption parameters, or unverifiable protected
data.



APP-SEC-RELEASE-DEBUG [GATE]

\- Release builds must not contain development-only
authentication bypasses, debug unlocks, test credentials,

  verbose secret
logging, development endpoints, or other intentional security bypasses.





